ll occur at low  ionic strength and solution at high  ionic strength zone six on the right  contains predominantly hydrophobic  ligands so binding will occur at  predominantly high ionic strength  Andalucian at low ionic strength and the  zones in the middle zones 2 3 4 5  contains mixtures of ionic and  hydrophobic groups organized into  predominantly anionic zones 2 &amp; 4 and  predominantly cationic zones three and  five groups the aliphatic hydrophobic  groups are gathered together in zones 2  &amp; 3 and the aromatic hydrophobic groups  are found in zones 4 &amp; 5 to demonstrate  the diversity of the mmm plate the  chemical composition of each ligand can  be analyzed with respect to various  physical or chemical properties the  distribution of hydrophobic and  hydrophilic accessible services is shown  in the upper t plots these descriptions  are described using the Schrodinger  sweet software as expected there is  significant variation of hydrophobic and  hydrophilic regions that correlate with  licken structure likewise a similarly  broad distribution of hydrogen bond  donor and acceptor groups is displayed  as shown in the lower two plots  properties can be analyzed in the same  way such as polarity aromaticity and  flexibility as well as predicted binding  to proteins it's interesting to note  that the similar patterns are displayed  for polarity flexibility and binding to  albumin this is a consequence of the  propensity of albumin to bind to long  flexible hydrocarbon chains or fatty  acids consequently analysis of these  chemical descriptors is a useful way of  confirming library diversity  this broad ligament diversity means it's  not possible to select a multimode  adsorbent with properties directly  suited to the purification in AD  due to its ease of use the screen rule  and adsorbent selection can be performed  very simply in a couple hours without  the need for expensive and complex  automated liquid handling systems  the enemy plates are prized a