 to a more complex medium human  plasma which contains many thousands of  different proteins a number of which our  interest as a therapeutic products for  use in protein replacement their  therapies the issue of protein  impurities in the context of human  plasma purification is interesting as  all the proteins are native to the human  however depending upon the application  for the purified plasma protein certain  certain protein impurities are  undesirable and need to be reduced to  very low concentrations for example  activated clotting factors are of a  concern and these the results in  thrombolytic effects if inadvertently  administered in significant  concentrations this is assuming of  course that the product is not a  clotting factor concentrated likewise  activated proteases can result in  uncontrolled bleeding episodes reducing  the concentration of undesirable plasma  proteins to acceptable levels can  present significant challenges and has  resulted in plasma product recalls in  the past consequently the mmm plates  have been used in a flow-through mode to  identify ligands capable of removing  specific problem impurities from the  product protein in this example the mmm  plate was screened for legumes which  bind Callie crime but not IgG IgG in  this case being used as the marker  protein the mmm plate was equilibrated  to the same connectivity and pH as that  of plasma and wonderlocke plasma was  loaded onto all the columns the plate  was washed to remove the nonviolent  material and a general additional  condition of a neutral buffer containing  1 molar salt and 10% hexane dial was  applied to all the columns although  several hits were observed which bound  Keller crime especially in zones 5  and that's denoted in a more red color  one ligand was identified g1 highlighted  in yellow which found 87 percent of the  Calla crime present but exhibited little  to no binding of IgG in another example  an Ann mmm plate was screened for  ligands capable of r